//! WordCraft on phones: the engine as a native library for the Android app in `android/`, with
//! bindings generated by [UniFFI](https://mozilla.github.io/uniffi-rs).
//!
//! The phone UI is one more frontend next to the desktop app, the CLI/MCP server and the web
//! build. Every edit is an engine command run by id ([`MobileSession::execute`]), so undo, the
//! never-crash guard and AutoCorrect behave as they do on the desktop. The engine lays the pages
//! out and `wordcraft-render` draws them to RGBA; the app shows them and draws the caret, the
//! selection and the keyboard's composing text over them from a [`SelectionView`].
//!
//! Positions on a page are in points (1/72 inch), y down, from the page's top left corner.
//!
//! Threading: every method may be called from any thread. The session lock is held for the
//! duration of a call (rendering draws after releasing it), so the UI calls them off its main
//! thread.
#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
#![deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic, clippy::unimplemented, clippy::todo, clippy::unreachable)]

use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, MutexGuard, PoisonError};

use serde_json::{Value, json};
